{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>ומחתה</b> — from מחיתי like כעב. And likewise the interpretation: four are they that are beyond me, and I did not know them in my wisdom." "Likewise the way of an adulterous woman — why does she not fear HaShem, for women are included among men, and just as she eats and wipes her mouth of food, so that it not be known that she ate, so she commits adultery and denies and says: I have done no iniquity, and a man must beware of her." "<b>אשה מנאפת</b> — Perhaps: her husband covers the matter with two, and another with three, and another with four."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {2 "The syntax is obscure; read hyper-literally. The passage may be corrupt or elliptical, and the argument compressed beyond certain resolution."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:25:37.640513423Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}